## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a scheduler that balances SLA guarantees with cost efficiency in a multi-tenant, cross-region LLM-ops environment.

## Key Concepts

- Quality of Service with per-tenant quotas and budgets
- Preemption mechanisms and priority queue management
- Cost modeling and real-time optimization dashboards
- Regional routing strategies and data locality considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: token-bucket burst control
function canSubmit(tenant) {
  const bucket = tenants[tenant];
  if (bucket.tokens > 0) {
    bucket.tokens--;
    return true;
  }
  return false;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests cost-aware routing and per-tenant quotas, a practical constraint in real llm-ops gateways.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant budgets and token accounting
- Routing policy using model variants (fast/balanced/cheap)
- Fallback mechanisms and caching
- API surface and minimal test plan

## Code Example

```javascript
function route(request, budget, models){
  const t = request.tokens;
  if (budget.remaining < t) return {model: models.cheap, useCache:true};
  // choose model based on remaining budget
  // ...
  return {model: models.balanced, remaining: budget.remaining - t};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test budget rollover at day boundary?
- How handle sudden budget spike without harming SLA?
